The vision-tactile-language-action model, post-training, evaluation, and serving
code is based on the OpenPI framework and has been modified by NeoteAI to
add tactile conditioning through predicted latent tactile tokens.

n0vtla/models_pytorch/transformers_replace/ contains modified copies of four files
from HuggingFace Transformers 4.53.2, Copyright Google Inc., Google AI, and the
HuggingFace Inc. team, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0:

    models/gemma/configuration_gemma.py    - modified
    models/gemma/modeling_gemma.py         - modified
    models/paligemma/modeling_paligemma.py - modified
    models/siglip/modeling_siglip.py       - modified

As required by Section 4(b) of that licence, we state that NeoteAI has changed these
files. The modifications add the adaptive RMSNorm (adaRMS) conditioning that the
action expert uses to inject the flow-matching timestep, drop the PaliGemma
image-feature rescaling, and align SigLIP dtype handling. The original copyright
headers are retained in each file.

models/siglip/check.py in that directory is not derived from Transformers; it is an
original installation check written for this project.

n0vtla/models/ contains code taken from Big Vision
(https://github.com/google-research/big_vision), Copyright 2024 Big Vision Authors
and Google LLC, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, with modifications.

DINOv2 (https://github.com/facebookresearch/dinov2) is used for tactile encoding
and LeRobot (https://github.com/huggingface/lerobot) for data handling, each under
their respective licenses.

